WEBVTT

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.013
From Start Here, choose Deploy a Cluster and select Foundation V M.

00:00:05.333 --> 00:00:08.277
Use this method when you have the classic Foundation virtual machine

00:00:08.533 --> 00:00:09.131
service.

00:00:09.472 --> 00:00:13.391
Foundation Central and standalone F C A are different backends.

00:00:13.641 --> 00:00:16.820
Review supported hardware and software for your environment.

00:00:17.097 --> 00:00:21.406
The guided journey opens existing workflows; moving between guidance stages

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.293
does not deploy a cluster or mark it verified.

00:00:24.862 --> 00:00:27.560
Open Cluster Create for Foundation V M.

00:00:27.826 --> 00:00:32.135
Enter the actual Foundation endpoint and service port, not a Prism address

00:00:32.306 --> 00:00:33.671
or browser page path.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.210
Select the required credential references.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.559
Confirm that the appliance can reach Foundation and the provisioning

00:00:39.644 --> 00:00:40.356
networks.

00:00:40.726 --> 00:00:42.667
Keep secrets in the credential store.

00:00:42.902 --> 00:00:47.296
Import a reviewed saved configuration when one exists, then inspect its

00:00:47.424 --> 00:00:50.051
targets rather than assuming the filename is correct.

00:00:50.526 --> 00:00:55.901
Stage the approved A H V and A O S installation files on Foundation, then

00:00:55.987 --> 00:00:58.184
refresh image inventory in the workflow.

00:00:58.462 --> 00:01:03.368
Choose the exact available filenames and supply the A H V I S O checksum

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:04.803
expected by Foundation.

00:01:05.086 --> 00:01:08.456
An image mounted somewhere else is not necessarily available to its

00:01:08.542 --> 00:01:09.267
installer.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:12.232
Review upload gates and capacity before staging.

00:01:12.552 --> 00:01:15.419
Resolve inventory or checksum errors before imaging.

00:01:15.861 --> 00:01:20.256
Review each node serial, block identity and position, host name, host

00:01:20.469 --> 00:01:23.520
address, controller address and management address.

00:01:23.797 --> 00:01:27.095
Select the appropriate node role and supported controller memory.

00:01:27.364 --> 00:01:32.399
Check per-node management credential references, subnet masks, gateways and

00:01:32.484 --> 00:01:33.551
V LAN settings.

00:01:33.807 --> 00:01:36.996
Re-foundation can overwrite existing installations.

00:01:37.412 --> 00:01:41.934
A valid form or selected hardware platform does not itself establish vendor

00:01:41.977 --> 00:01:44.452
compatibility or permission to erase a node.

00:01:44.878 --> 00:01:47.387
Save the configuration and run Dry Run.

00:01:47.676 --> 00:01:51.943
Review the native schema checks, selected images, connectivity and

00:01:51.986 --> 00:01:54.418
credential findings that the workflow provides.

00:01:54.674 --> 00:01:56.030
Fix every blocker.

00:01:56.319 --> 00:01:59.860
Review the generated target list and obtain approval for the exact

00:02:00.031 --> 00:02:02.271
configuration where policy requires it.

00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:05.399
Enter the required deployment confirmation deliberately.

00:02:05.732 --> 00:02:09.785
Saving, importing and approving are separate from actually selecting Run

00:02:09.828 --> 00:02:10.482
Workflow.

00:02:10.852 --> 00:02:14.436
Submit once, then follow the linked job and Foundation session.

00:02:14.735 --> 00:02:18.650
Read phase and node progress, logs and actual target state.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:22.778
A missing response or interrupted browser is not a reason to submit imaging

00:02:22.906 --> 00:02:23.332
again.

00:02:23.546 --> 00:02:27.770
After Foundation finishes, confirm cluster identity and membership.

00:02:27.983 --> 00:02:30.232
Continue to reviewed post-configuration.

00:02:30.603 --> 00:02:34.955
When initial access needs a password and EULA bootstrap, use the supported

00:02:35.126 --> 00:02:38.282
bootstrap sequence before the required health verification.
